  "question": {
    "text": "If <math> <mi>f</mi><mfenced> <mi>x</mi> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup> <mfenced> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> <mrow> <mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow> </msup> </math>, then <math> <msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>′</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mn>0</mn> </mfenced> </math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow>  <mn>2</mn><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow>  <mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow>  <mn>3</mn><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x2212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "By taking logarithm on both sides,<math>&#160;</math><br /><mrow><span style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</span><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><span style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</span> </mfenced></mrow><br />On differentiating, we get,&nbsp;<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />Now, put <math> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>0)</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced> <mrow> <mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced> <mn>0</mn> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math>"
  }
